 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "InspectionAdvisor ⊣ Fire-Risk Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph,
 append-only audit ledger. A fire-risk-inspection BACK-OFFICE
 COORDINATION actor for an independent inspection contractor -- not
 direct inspection-robot-actuation authority (beyond passive sensing)
 and not a fire-department-dispatch authority. Four ops
 (`:log-inspection` / `:fire-hazard-survey` / `:escalate-hazard` /
 `:schedule-reinspection`), all `:effect :propose` only. Twelve
 concrete governor checks: propose-only effect, closed op allowlist,
 closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct hardware control),
 permanent equipment-actuate block, permanent dispatch-authority
 side-channel block (this actor never self-reports a fire-department
 dispatch outside the gated hazard-escalation path), independent site
 verification/registration before any survey or reinspection schedule,
 independent recompute of the elevated/normal finding from the raw
 hazard-score sensor reading against the site's own registered
 threshold (never trusting a proposal's own self-reported finding),
 hazard-score plausibility validation, independent on-file-elevated-
 finding gate before any reinspection may be scheduled (or billed),
 double-schedule guard, and survey-type validation (closed set:
 `:building` / `:vegetation` / `:fire-protection-system`, the latter
 two grounded in real NFPA standards -- NFPA 25 for fixed
 water-based fire-protection-system inspection, NFPA 1141 for
 wildland/rural/suburban vegetation-interface fire-protection
 infrastructure -- cited only for the survey-type taxonomy, never for
 a fabricated numeric threshold). Hazard escalation (an active hazard
 requiring immediate fire-department dispatch, the exact scenario this
 README names) ALWAYS escalates to a human dispatcher;
 `:log-inspection` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at
 phase 3 when governor-clean."}
